description:
In wp11_pkcs11.c C_Verify, the function checks pData and pSignature are not NULL but does NOT validate that ulSignatureLen is nonzero. PKCS#11 2.40 requires verification to fail gracefully on a zero-length signature. The backend verify() receives size_t ulSignatureLen=0 and may read uninitialized memory or misbehave depending on implementation.

Trigger: Call C_VerifyInit (valid), then C_Verify with ulSignatureLen=0 and a valid non-NULL pSignature pointer.
Research needed: Confirm whether any backend's verify() is safe against zero-length signatures, or whether it will dereference past the end of a zero-length buffer. If unsafe, add: if (ulSignatureLen == 0) { rv = CKR_SIGNATURE_INVALID; goto cleanup; }
